Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:17:10 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Record complete Linux test environment requirements

Prepared with AI assistance. Include curl and preserve LF source text for Linux-based verification.
---
 local-build/Dockerfile | 2 +-
 local-build/README.md  | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/local-build/Dockerfile b/local-build/Dockerfile
index 9f548b6..855f75b 100644
--- a/local-build/Dockerfile
+++ b/local-build/Dockerfile
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 FROM oven/bun:1@sha256:3aa040e5445efa09d75bb428a64ba50db13e2b3ac9b6b0c7f145615f62b2ee18 AS bun
 FROM rust:slim-bookworm@sha256:7c7d4eb4d05b7781187a327809466cfddf29753f6defdc3d19a0e291951b7a37
-RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends gcc-mingw-w64-x86-64-posix binutils-mingw-w64-x86-64 pkg-config ca-certificates git nodejs chromium && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
+RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends gcc-mingw-w64-x86-64-posix binutils-mingw-w64-x86-64 pkg-config ca-certificates curl git nodejs chromium && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
 RUN rustup target add x86_64-pc-windows-gnu
 COPY --from=bun /usr/local/bin/bun /usr/local/bin/bun
 ENV CARGO_TARGET_X86_64_PC_WINDOWS_GNU_LINKER=x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc
diff --git a/local-build/README.md b/local-build/README.md
index 41022db..b9db81e 100644
--- a/local-build/README.md
+++ b/local-build/README.md
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ Read [LOCAL-REVIEW.md](LOCAL-REVIEW.md) for the Windows worker limitations. On t
 
 The Dockerfile pins its two base-image digests. It installs Rust build dependencies, a Windows GNU cross-compiler, Bun, and Chromium inside the container. No account keys or home-directory mounts are needed. Keep build caches in disposable Docker volumes, not in the source archive.
 
-1. Apply the accompanying patch to the exact upstream base. Check out Markdown with LF line endings; CRLF inflates upstream's byte-budget checks.
+1. Apply the accompanying patch to the exact upstream base. Use `core.autocrlf=false` for this Linux build checkout; CRLF breaks shell shebangs, workflow assertions, and byte-budget checks. Windows `.cmd` launchers must retain CRLF.
 2. Build `local-build/Dockerfile` and mount only this checkout at `/src` plus a Cargo target cache at `/src/target`.
 3. Run `cargo +stable test --locked -p impeccable-live worker_permission_tests`, then the workspace tests. Chromium tests run in the isolated container; `chromium-test` is a container-only wrapper for root CI. Never install that wrapper as your normal browser.
 4. Build `cargo +stable build --locked --release --target x86_64-pc-windows-gnu -p impeccable`. Export `target/x86_64-pc-windows-gnu/release/impeccable.exe` to `local-build/artifacts/impeccable.exe`.
